    "source_sha256": "c156c48416bba9c3ca3fa7fbf38f5059df92eecf4940555c0a8fd198e5f8b3fa",
    "verbatim": "**F-10 (specimen hazard, inherent to `/1` and not an adapter bug). The installment invoice lets any third party drain escrow into fees.**\n`partial` debits only ScriptCustodied `escrow`, so it needs no signer (CB-4/CB-7). Starting after `open` (escrow 109, invoice 90, reserve 14):\n\n| Step | Effect |\n|---|---|\n| Each `partial(1)` call | Moves 2 to `fees` and 1 to `seller`. |\n| After 36 calls | Escrow is 1 and invoice is 54. |\n| 37th `partial` | Refuses on `balance`. |\n| `finish` | Also refuses on `balance`. |\n\nThe thread is then permanently stuck: the seller is short 54, the buyer's reserve of 14 is unfunded, and `fees` gained 72 [INF from source plus OR numbers]. This is correct `/1` behaviour under CB-6/CB-7, but it must be disclosed. The specimen must not be described as a safe escrow. Correction: R5S-18."
  }
